WEBVTT

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.730
Akira!

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.940
What is it, Sis?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.820
I found it!

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.410
Sis...

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.260
What are you wearing?

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.910
It’s for the festival tonight!

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.040
There’s a festival at the Kazami Shrine. Remember?

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.900
Oh, that’s right. The summer festival is today.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.990
Here, put this on!

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:33.800
Huh?

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.500
It’s for the festival, silly!

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.150
You should wear a yukata too!

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.820
I’ll pass.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.100
You loved wearing them as a kid!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.960
You pretended to be a samurai.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.230
That's ancient history.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.940
Whatever! Just put this on and bring along a crush or something!

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.890
Guys and girls both get excited when they see each other in a new outfit.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.160
I wonder if Urabe would come along if I asked.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.970
"A Mysterious
Summer Festival"

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.820
I also brought your sandals out.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.480
Thanks.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.200
Try not to get lost.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.960
I always end up having to spend the entire night looking for you.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.360
I keep telling you, that’s ancient history.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.490
Bye! I’ll see you later.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.880
See you later.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.860
I wonder who she’s going with.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.000
'Sup!

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.250
Tsubaki?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.270
Ueno?

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.400
My friend!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.330
What?

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.660
Tsubaki, my man!

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.700
You got all geared up knowing I'd come get you!

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.560
What are you talking about?

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:43.960
Am I wrong?

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.830
That yukata tells me you can’t wait to go to the festival.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.500
My sister made me wear this!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.210
That’s cool.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.300
Now, let me ask you again.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.000
Tsubaki, come with me to the festival!

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.780
Hell no. Why would I go with a guy?

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.660
Whoops, not what I meant.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.390
Come with <i>us to the festival!</i>

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.010
“Us”?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:12.770
Yeah, well, I sorta asked out my girlfriend, Oka.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:16.730
But we can’t have our classmates seeing the two of us alone in public.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:22.570
So we plan to start off the evening with a group of four in order to create a good alibi!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.610
Four?

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.720
Tsubaki, this is your big chance!

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.910
The girl we're bringing along is totally your type.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.760
Who might that be?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.970
Oka’s bringing Urabe with her.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.330
Leave everything to me!

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:43.670
Let’s double date!

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.560
Oh, there they are!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.690
Hey, sorry we’re late!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.190
Gulp!

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:07.700
Sorry! It took longer than we thought to get dressed.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.280
Did you wait long?

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.880
No, not at all! Right?

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.720
Huh?

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.530
O-Oh, yeah.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.330
Really? Thank god!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.990
Holy crap! My girlfriend’s too cute!

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.300
She’s cute!

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.510
Urabe!

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.460
Now that we’re all here,

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.240
let’s take a photo!

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:41.240
Wonderful! That yukata looks great on you...

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.510
Y-You think so?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.550
Urabe-san!

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:47.070
Let me take some of Urabe-san by herself!

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.600
Uh, sure.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.120
Beautiful!

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.580
This time with the town as the backdrop!

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.080
Perfect!

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.880
That yukata makes you look like you fell straight from heaven!

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.170
What the hell’s this?

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.810
Urabe-san, you’re so cute!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.130
Beats me.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.890
The festival held at the end of every summer at Kazami Shrine

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.900
always ends with a firework display.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.900
It’s a pretty big event in our town.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.110
That’s a strange design.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.810
Maybe it’s her yukata,

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:44.500
but she looks more mature than usual.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.490
Ugh, it's so crowded.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.490
It'll be even worse when the fireworks start.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.320
Yeah.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:59.140
Now that I think about it, all four of us together like this is kind of weird.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.940
I know that Ueno and Oka are in a relationship,

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.960
but he has no idea about me and Urabe.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.410
I wonder how much she's told Oka.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:17.160
Well, I don’t think Oka knows about us either.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.940
Hey, Urabe-san,

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:23.090
does Tsubaki-kun know that I know about you two?

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:25.170
No, I don’t think so.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.440
I swear, guys can be pretty clueless.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.130
Do you want a bite?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.640
Your face was irresistible just then!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:46.570
Oka-san, you’ll end up getting lost in the crowd if you keep doing that.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:51.030
If me and Ueno-kun get lost, that means you get Tsubaki-kun all to yourself!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.300
That’s not what I’m hoping for.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.420
Oh, I just remembered,

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:04.580
there’s this amazing thing that you're only able to buy here tonight!

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.840
Tsubaki!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.800
Tonight, I’m going to...

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.340
score with Oka!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.780
I’m doing it!

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.230
Look at that!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.160
That red bracelet!

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:28.490
It’s a love charm that you can buy at Kazami Shrine!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.410
A love charm.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:35.120
If your girlfriend ties that bracelet on your wrist,

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.240
it’ll take your relationship to another level!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:44.210
The day after I bought that charm, me and Oka kissed!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:51.590
However, you can only buy it tonight during the festival.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:52.880
Listen, Tsubaki!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:56.360
Just take my word for it and buy it!

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.020
I'd get to kiss Urabe?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.480
Tsubaki-kun.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.940
I could really use that charm!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:17.060
You can hear opportunity knocking, right, Tsubaki?

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:21.180
I'll drag Oka off and end this double date.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.080
Then I'm going to...

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.780
score!

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.580
Did you want me, Ueno-kun?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.160
You can see the fireworks better from over there.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.150
Let’s go.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.740
The place is marked with the shrine’s fox masks, got it?

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.390
That’s where you buy the charm!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.260
Come on, let’s go!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.370
Adiós, Tsubaki!

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.260
H-Hey!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.390
Oka-san?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.310
Ueno!

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.770
What’s gotten into them?

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:58.670
Did they plan this from the start?

00:09:58.670 --> 00:09:59.870
Plan?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.310
Er, forget what I said.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.420
Okay.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:09.920
So, uh, Urabe... good evening.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.290
Good evening, Tsubaki-kun.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:19.060
God, Urabe is so cute in her yukata.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:22.420
That yukata—

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.100
Sorry, what is it, Urabe?

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.850
No, you go ahead.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.920
Oh, er... nothing.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.260
Really?

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.710
We need to find those two.

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.540
Yeah, we got separated.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:46.870
I'd rather spend this time with you alone, though.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.620
But there’s a place I want to go first.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.040
Huh? Really?

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:57.170
Actually, I was kinda thinking the same thing.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.450
The firework show's about to begin.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.560
Urabe!

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:11.080
Tsubaki-kun!

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.730
Come here!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.070
Where are—

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:27.740
The charm you can only buy tonight is over here!

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.170
Huh?

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.440
This is strange.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.830
Where did she go?

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.140
Urabe!

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:52.640
What's that?

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.490
Is this a...

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.940
freak show tent?

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:05.960
Not a charm shop?

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.160
Is Urabe in here?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:15.160
I can't even see my hands.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.320
What's this?

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:24.030
This is... Urabe’s!

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.330
All right.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:28.890
What’s that?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.820
Urabe!

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:49.790
Tsubaki-kun.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.700
What are you doing up there?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.840
Hang on, I’ll get you down!

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.370
Only one chance.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.300
You only get one chance at the String Pull.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.620
String Pull?

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.290
You don't know what a String Pull is?

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.810
It’s that thing over there.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.310
There are prizes at the ends of certain strings.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:17.600
Well, I guess you can say it’s like drawing lots.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.400
You only get one pull.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:27.900
If you don’t pick the string attached to her, it’ll spell disaster.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:31.100
Disaster?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:36.750
She wandered in here while we were setting up and got caught in the strings.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.360
That means that it's not complete yet.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:44.170
If you pull the wrong string, everything will come tumbling down...

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.720
with a crash!

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.710
No way!

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.310
Urabe!

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.980
Ow!

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.900
Don’t look up my clothes!

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:02.320
This isn't the time or place for that, Urabe!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.150
Don’t look, got it?!

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:07.330
What’s the big deal over showing some panties?

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.750
Your girlfriend must be a piece of work.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:15.400
I only get one pull, but I can’t even get close?

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.290
What am I supposed to do?

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:21.540
Tsubaki-kun, pull the string you like the most.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.050
But...

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:30.550
Don’t worry. We share a very strong bond.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.810
Urabe.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.220
What is she doing?

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.850
I can see it!

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:11.590
Now what? What should I do?

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.150
I gotta connect with her more!

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:16.850
I know!

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.100
With this!

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.360
Urabe!

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:29.990
I see it!

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.960
Urabe’s drool...

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.720
So sweet!

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:06.610
The string that’s connected to Urabe...

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:11.280
is this one!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.240
We got a winner!

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:23.330
Urabe!

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.830
Tsubaki-kun!

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:26.960
Urabe!

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.130
Sorry, Urabe!

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.260
Tsubaki-kun.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.030
Thank you, thank you! That was great!

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:46.100
That isn’t something you see every day. Thank you.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.080
Hope you enjoy your night!

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:03.140
Where’s the freak show tent?

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:07.410
Are we at Kazami Shrine?

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:09.020
I think so.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:12.590
What were we doing? Was it a dream?

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:15.220
My butt still hurts, though.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:18.360
Oh right, are you okay?

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:19.760
Yeah.

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.620
Sorry, I let it slip out of my hands.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:28.010
Your yukata’s all dirty!

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:33.740
Weren’t there some patterns right here?

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.160
Tsubaki-kun!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.990
Sorry, I wasn’t thinking!

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:42.620
Not the panty scissors!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.870
I forgot.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.120
What’s up?

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:52.500
I’m...

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.000
not wearing any underwear.

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:01.410
S-So... that means...

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:05.320
you’re... naked under that yukata?

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:06.430
Yeah.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:10.080
So I’m keeping my scissors here.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.250
So that’s why you told me not to look up.

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:17.200
Yeah.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:22.570
That must be why the drool on that string was extra sweet.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:26.970
Still, what was she thinking, leaving herself exposed like that?

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:29.920
Actually, that reminds me...

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:32.250
God.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:37.010
I got all sweaty looking for you!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.510
Akira!

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.660
I’m taking a bath!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:51.560
My sister didn’t wear anything under her yukata either.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.450
Tsubaki-kun, what’s wrong?

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.590
Oh, uh, don’t worry about it.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:02.280
In any case, how did you end up all the way here?

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:04.400
Well...

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.920
Were you going to buy a love charm?

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:19.170
Oka-san told me you can only get them tonight.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.350
Urabe!

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:25.320
Since we’re here, let’s buy one!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.060
Wait, Tsubaki-kun!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.190
Look.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.550
Oh, you already bought one?

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:37.540
No, one got tied to my scissors somehow.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:40.940
Wow, talk about a mystery.

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:42.950
Tsubaki-kun, let me see your hand.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.310
Sure.

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:54.950
Probably a present from the love charm god.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.670
Thanks, Urabe.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.170
Sure.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.270
Urabe, where are you shoes?

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.570
They fell off my feet.

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:13.590
I’m carrying you. You can’t walk barefooted, can you?

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.950
Y-You don’t have to do that!

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:34.080
Urabe, grab on tight, just to be safe.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:40.630
Her boobs are pressed against my back!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.070
They’re so soft and warm!

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:46.390
No, never mind that!

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:53.290
I wonder who those two in the fox masks were.

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.370
Yeah.

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.420
Must've either been a dream or an illusion.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:03.610
Or a couple of fox spirits.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:14.370
Matsubue-kun, a high school kid can’t drink!

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:16.540
It’s just water.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:17.630
Oh.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:18.890
Geez.

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:24.960
So all you wanted was the cup and bottle that was on that girl’s butt?

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:26.780
Yeah, I guess.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:30.810
That’s a rare fabric from the Middle Edo period, you know.

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:31.810
Wow!

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:35.560
Don't worry. I made sure to thank her.

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:39.950
I’ll have a drink too.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.860
Whoa there.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:46.960
That was great! Now I’m drunk!

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:48.940
Off water?

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:52.540
Geez, I guess any girlfriend is a piece of work.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.010
Hey, Togawa.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:56.040
What?

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:59.130
Can I drink your tears?

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.520
Huh, my tears?

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:04.850
I got the onion extract right here.

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:07.050
No need for that.

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:10.960
Geez, he’s always making strange requests.

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:12.510
Let’s see...

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:16.890
Aw, summer is about to end.

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:21.000
Oh, there you go, Matsubue-kun.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:24.220
Thanks a bunch, Togawa. Really.

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.410
You know, Matsubue-kun,

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:35.750
I’m going to keep fulfilling your requests until I solve your mystery.

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:39.030
Why did I fall in love with you?

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:49.510
I’m sure I’ll solve that mystery of mine once I solve yours.

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:57.680
The mystery that entangles everyone who falls in love.

00:23:17.030 --> 00:23:18.510
Oka...

00:23:18.510 --> 00:23:19.570
Don’t!

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:22.200
It'll fall off if I move.

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:43.440
I... I...

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:48.180
scored a hug off Oka, Tsubaki!

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:51.530
Tsubaki-kun.

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:52.780
What?

00:23:55.690 --> 00:23:56.790
What is it?

00:23:57.430 --> 00:23:58.530
So...

00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:01.510
Here. Today’s portion.

00:24:01.510 --> 00:24:02.580
Oh.

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:04.810
Thanks.

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:11.800
Urabe, next year—

00:24:20.100 --> 00:24:21.820
It's beautiful.

00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:22.910
Yeah.

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:30.990
If it weren't for the fireworks, our hearts would be beating loud enough for other people to hear.

00:24:32.270 --> 00:24:36.790
Well, it <i>has been one crazy and mysterious summer festival.</i>

00:24:37.340 --> 00:24:39.580
But next year, just the two of us...

00:24:40.350 --> 00:24:42.690
Hey, Tsubaki-kun.

00:24:42.690 --> 00:24:44.470
Hm? What?

00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:48.380
Let’s come back next year, just the two of us.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:50.830
Sure!
